You might ask why we need title and accessibilities, langium entry rule must have an assignment, so we can't have empty AST, that's why I added those.

> Not sure why :)

Because that's how errors should generally be handled. (Unless there is a need to return without throwing)
Pseudo code below. 

```ts
// somewhere inside mermaid
import { parse } from 'mermaid-parser';
const parseText = (text: string) => {
  try {
    const { ast, type } = await parse(text);
//    log(Got type with ast);
    return { ast, type };
  } catch (error) {
// Type check here. 
    const { parserErrors, lexerErrors } = error.details;
    log.error(
      error.details,
      'Error parsing diagram'
    );
    throw new MermaidParsingError(parserErrors, lexerErrors);
  }
}

